   $q$Priya rides a Ferris wheel with a diameter of 40 meters whose center is 22 meters above the ground. It makes one full turn every 12 minutes, and Priya boards at the lowest point at $t = 0$. Which function gives Priya's height $h$, in meters, after $t$ minutes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$h(t) = 20 - 22\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-amplitude-and-midline"},{"text":"$h(t) = 22 - 20\\cos(12t)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-period-as-coefficient"},{"text":"$h(t) = 22 - 20\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$h(t) = 22 - 40\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-diameter-as-amplitude"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$h(t) = 22 - 20\cos\left(\frac{\pi t}{6}\right)$$q$, $q$The midline is the center height 22, the amplitude is the radius 20, $b = \frac{2\pi}{12} = \frac{\pi}{6}$, and $-\cos$ starts at the minimum, giving $h(0) = 2$. The choice with $40$ uses the diameter, which would send Priya 18 meters below ground.$q$, 'draft', null)
