   $q$A game designer rotates a character's position $90^\circ$ counterclockwise about the origin by multiplying by $R = \begin{bmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 \end{bmatrix}$. The character starts at $(3, 5)$. Where does it end up?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(5, -3)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-transpose-rotated-clockwise"},{"text":"$(-5, -3)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"},{"text":"$(-5, 3)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(-3, 5)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"negated-without-swapping"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(-5, 3)$$q$, $q$$R\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\ 5 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 0(3) - 1(5) \\ 1(3) + 0(5) \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} -5 \\ 3 \end{bmatrix}$, so the point moves to $(-5, 3)$. The choice $(5, -3)$ is a clockwise turn, which comes from using the columns of $R$ as rows.$q$, 'draft', null)
