   $q$A game designer builds a spinner where a player gains 6 points with probability $p$, gains 1 point with probability $0.5$, and loses 4 points with probability $0.5 - p$. For the game to be fair, what must $p$ be?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-loss-probability-as-one-half"},{"text":"$0.75$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-distribute-negative"},{"text":"$0.2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-middle-outcome"},{"text":"$0.15$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.15$$q$, $q$Set $6p + 1(0.5) - 4(0.5 - p) = 0$, so $6p + 0.5 - 2 + 4p = 0$, giving $10p = 1.5$ and $p = 0.15$. The choice $0.75$ writes $-4(0.5 - p)$ as $-2 - 4p$, failing to distribute the negative sign.$q$, 'draft', null)
