   $q$A phone warranty costs 90 dollars. Without it, there is a $0.2$ chance of a 250 dollar screen repair and, independently, a $0.1$ chance of a 120 dollar battery repair. Which decision has the lower expected cost, and by how much?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Buy the warranty, by $280$ dollars","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-probabilities"},{"text":"Buy the warranty, by $21$ dollars","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pooled-probabilities-and-costs"},{"text":"Skip the warranty, by $62$ dollars","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-expected-cost-not-difference"},{"text":"Skip the warranty, by $28$ dollars","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Skip the warranty, by $28$ dollars$q$, $q$Expected repair cost $= 0.2(250) + 0.1(120) = 50 + 12 = 62$ dollars, which is $90 - 62 = 28$ dollars less than the warranty. The choice Buy by 21 multiplies the combined probability $0.3$ by the combined cost 370, which is not how expected value works.$q$, 'draft', null)
