   $q$On a practice test, each question has 5 choices. A correct answer earns 1 point and a wrong answer loses $\frac{1}{4}$ point. Bilal rules out one wrong choice and guesses at random among the rest. What is Bilal's expected score on that question?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-eliminated-choice"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{16}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$-\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-full-point-penalty"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-penalty"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{1}{16}$$q$, $q$With 4 choices left, $E = \frac{1}{4}(1) + \frac{3}{4}\left(-\frac{1}{4}\right) = \frac{4}{16} - \frac{3}{16} = \frac{1}{16}$, so guessing now helps on average. The choice $0$ is the expected score of a blind guess among all 5 choices.$q$, 'draft', null)
