insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8d564f08-17dd-5a1e-a86b-4fd51bbf287b', 'rg4-context-clues-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Orange Fish Kite$q$, $q$Kenji had spent three evenings building a kite for Kite Day at Willow Park. He glued the paper, tied the string, and painted a bright orange fish on the front. Now he stood on the hill, eager to see it fly. He could hardly wait.

He ran across the grass, and the kite rose a few feet. Then it wobbled, flipped over, and plunged straight down into the grass. Kenji groaned. He tried again and again, but each time the kite crashed.

"Maybe it's too heavy," said his older sister, Hana. "Let's examine it." The two of them knelt down and looked closely at every part of the kite. Hana pointed to the tail. It was made of thick cloth and was as long as Kenji was tall.

"That tail is weighing it down," she said. Kenji frowned, because he was proud of that tail. Still, he was willing to try anything. He cut off the cloth tail and tied on a light strip of paper instead.

This time, a strong gust of wind rushed suddenly across the hill, and the kite soared. It climbed higher and higher until the orange fish was a tiny dot in the sky. Kenji laughed. His frown had vanished, and a wide grin had taken its place.$q$, 'draft')
