-- Passage rg4-context-clues-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('bd93c638-a73d-51fe-964a-a0ff0d01b307', 'rg4-context-clues-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Saturday at the Market$q$, $q$Every Saturday, Dmitri helped his grandfather sell apples at the farmers market. Grandpa Ivan had a small stall, a wooden table under a green tent, at the end of the row.

This Saturday, the market was bustling. Crowds of shoppers filled the paths, and people called out to friends as they hurried from table to table. Dmitri had never seen so many people in one place.

A woman picked up an apple and turned it over in her hand. "Are these crisp or soft?" she asked.

"Crisp," said Dmitri. "They crunch loudly when you bite them." He sliced a piece so she could taste it. She smiled and bought a whole bag.

By noon, the apples were nearly gone. Only a few bruised ones were left at the bottom of the basket. Dmitri thought nobody would want them. But Grandpa had a plan. "We won't toss these," he said. "Bruised apples are perfect for applesauce. We will cook them tonight."

On the way home, Dmitri carried the empty baskets. His feet were sore after the long day. Grandpa put a hand on his shoulder. "You were a big help today," he said. Dmitri felt a warm glow of pride, and he forgot all about his tired feet.$q$, 'draft')
